World Monitor CLI is a command-line client for the World Monitor global
intelligence API.  It shows a terminal dashboard with country briefs, risk
scores and conflict, cyber, market, climate and infrastructure feeds, and
it installs the commands worldmonitor and wm.

Most data commands require a subscription API key of worldmonitor.app in the
WORLDMONITOR_API_KEY environment variable.
The terminal dashboard also starts without a key, using public bootstrap
data.  The client talks to the hosted service at worldmonitor.app, it does
not connect to a self-hosted installation.  It is independent of the port
www/worldmonitor, which installs the self-hosted dashboard.
